{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfjyVTXGpNoeGCS4r1XkA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q71GVoavitRebHxmEJZ2cr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/jcole/projects/hq/.night-crew/runs/20261006/worktrees/identity-code-and-qr/.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/merge-intents/identity-code-and-qr.md","content":"# Merge intent — Card 1 (E1) · `identity-code-and-qr`\n\nRun `20261006` · loop-owned branch `night-crew/20261006/identity-code-and-qr` off `dev` at\n`efcd970` · roadmap Activity E card E1 (one permanent identity code per customer, as a QR the\nshipped scanner reads offline and online). Card 2 (`mms-send-on-signup`, the MMS send) builds on\nthis card's merged tip. Written before any implementation; the \"Facts at the end of the card\"\nsection at the bottom is appended when the card finishes.\n\n## Shared files touched (outside the card's own packages)\n\n| File | Why |\n|---|---|\n| `backend/internal/marketing/subscribers.go` | Slate-named shared surface. `ImportSubscribers` mints an identity code for every NEW subscriber after its import transaction commits; the import result gains `warnings`; `GET /subscribers/{id}` reports `identity_code.status` as `not_minted / minted / sent` plus `identity_code.media_url`. **Signature change:** `ImportSubscribers(ctx, pool, imp)` → `ImportSubscribers(ctx, d Deps, imp)` — the mint needs the QR base URL and the projection config, and Card 2 needs the sender from the same struct. |\n| `backend/internal/marketing/routes.go` | Slate-named shared surface. `GET` + `HEAD /m/{id}.png` under `MountPublic`, beside `/q/{short}`. |\n| `backend/internal/marketing/projection.go` | Slate-named, this card is the solo owner tonight. Adds `ProjectIdentityCode` beside `ProjectCampaign`. No egress-allowlist change: the file is already on the list for its PostgREST client. |\n| `backend/internal/marketing/subscribers_test.go` | (a) the eight `ImportSubscribers(ctx, pool, …)` call sites take `testDeps(pool)`; (b) ONE assertion moves from `not_sent` to `minted` — an imported subscriber now has a code, and the spec's status set no longer contains `not_sent`. The egress allowlist in this file is NOT edited. |\n| `tests/marketing-subscribers.spec.js` | The same one assertion (`identity_code.status` `not_sent` → `minted`) for the same reason. The on-screen text the spec checks (\"not sent yet\") is unchanged — `marketing/subscribers.js` treats every status other than `sent` as not sent, and this card does not edit that file (it is Card 2's). |\n| `marketing.html` | Slate-named: ONE line, `#scan-file-surface` 320 → 640 px. Any other diff in this file is not this card's. |\n| `playwright.config.js` | **Outside the slate's footprint table — stated, not a park.** The `webServer` command gains `HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH=internal/marketing/sources/testdata/fluentforms_submissions.json` so the e2e stack's `POST /subscribers/import/web-form` reads the committed fixture. The gate says \"import the fixture with `HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH`\"; the variable is read from the SERVER's environment, and without this line `[IC-01]` would pass only when the person launching Playwright remembered to export it — and would red on the orchestrator's full suite. No existing spec drives the web-form route, so nothing else changes behaviour. A stack hand-provisioned behind `NIGHTCREW_ENV_URL` must export the same variable; the spec fails with that sentence if the import answers `503 ff_not_configured`. |\n| `night-crew.toml` | Comment only: the `marketing` seam's roll call moves 7 → 8 (`marketing-identity.spec.js` joins by filename). **No key, no token.** |\n| `.night-crew/knowledge/roadmap.md` | This card's own Activity E line: `PLANNED` → `LANDED` (the orchestrator adds the merge SHA). Append-only otherwise. |\n| `.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/merge-intents/identity-code-and-qr.md` | This note. |\n| `.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/logs/identity-code-and-qr/*` | Red / green / gate logs with commands and exit lines. |\n\nInside the footprint (new files): `backend/internal/db/migrations/0088_identity_codes.sql`,\n`backend/internal/marketing/identity.go`, `identity_test.go`, `backend/cmd/qrgen/main.go`\n(a small dev/test generator re-homed from the spike's `qrgen.go` — `[IC-03]` needs a\nMedium-correction PNG \"generated in-test\" and the repo has no Node QR encoder; it is not built\ninto the server image, which compiles `./cmd/server` only), `tests/marketing-identity.spec.js`.\n\n**Not touched:** `sw.js` and `version.json` (generated from git HEAD — the orchestrator\nregenerates at the merged HEAD; this card adds and removes no precached file, count stays 51),\n`backend/internal/marketing/helpers_test.go` (Card 2's), `backend/cmd/server/main.go` (Card 2's),\n`marketing/subscribers.js` (Card 2's), `marketing/scanner.js` and `parseEmbeddedOffer` (the reader\nis untouched — the descriptor contract is the shipped one), migrations `0083`–`0087`, anything\nunder `.night-crew/qa/`, any `scan_attempts` status or submit-machine pair.\n\n## What must survive any merge\n\n1. **The encoding: `qrcode.New(payload, qrcode.Low)` at 512 px, a 16-character token, date-only\n   `expires_at`.** The spike measured the shipped reader failing on denser symbols; \"upgrading\" to\n   Medium makes the code unreadable from a photo. `[IC-03]` is the control for exactly this.\n2. **The raw token exists only inside the PNG.** `subscribers.identity_token_hash` holds\n   `hex(sha256(token))`; no log line, event, response body or column carries the token.\n3. **`/m/{id}.png` is mounted by `MountPublic`** (root router, no session) — a customer's phone\n   and, in Card 2, the carrier fetch the image with no HQ login. Moving it under `Mount` breaks\n   both. Its only secret is the unguessable media id.\n4. **The mint happens AFTER the import transaction commits, one subscriber per transaction**, and\n   a projection that is unconfigured or failing never rolls a mint back: the import answers 200\n   with `warnings:[\"not_projected\"]`.\n5. **Identity-only codes (no first-touch campaign) are never projected** and their payload has no\n   `#o=` fragment. Which campaign such a signup is entitled to is an operator question (the\n   card's PARK note); nothing here guesses one.\n6. **`identity_media.subscriber_id … ON DELETE CASCADE`** — deleting a subscriber deletes their\n   image; that is the erasure path.\n7. **Migration number `0088`**, with its Down.\n8. Card 2 extends `ImportSubscribers` AFTER this card's mint loop; the `signed_up` insert path and\n   the `resend_requested` event are unchanged by this card.\n\n## What is safe to drop\n\n`backend/cmd/qrgen/` is safe to drop only together with `[IC-03]` (its one caller). The evidence\nlogs are safe to drop in the sense that no suite reads them. Nothing else.\n\n## done_when clauses — stubs and fixtures\n\n**The sender stub is the point tonight (D-KR2), and this card has no sender at all**: it mints,\nrenders and projects; nothing is sent, no provider is called, and\n`TestNothingInThisPackageSends` stays green with no allowlist change. Per clause:\n\n| Clause | Rides a stub or fixture? |\n|---|---|\n| `[IC-01]` offline scan of the server-minted PNG → `embeddedOffer` | **Fixture input, real path.** Subscribers come from the committed Fluent Forms fixture (`HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH`), never the live website database; the campaign and its code are seeded by SQL on the e2e database (:5434). The mint, the PNG, the public route and the shipped scanner page are all real. No sender involved. |\n| `[IC-02]` the same PNG online → `offerReady`, source `server` | **Stub — the one permitted one.** The server lookup is answered by `page.route` on the sync door's path (the e2e stack has no substrate), returning the row the projection would have written (id = the uuid-v5 of the subscriber id, the campaign, its `ends_at`). The projection itself is NOT exercised here — `TestProjectIdentityCodeUpserts` covers it against a fake PostgREST. No sender involved. |\n| `[IC-03]` negative control (Medium / version 11) | No stub. The PNG is generated in-test by `backend/cmd/qrgen` with the repo's own `go-qrcode`, scanned through the shipped page. |\n| `TestMintIdentityCodeIsIdempotent`, `TestMintIdentityCodeNoFirstTouchIsIdentityOnly` | No stub. Real Postgres on :5434 (`hq_test_go_e1`). Projection deliberately unconfigured in the second. |\n| `TestProjectIdentityCodeUpserts` | **Stub: an `httptest` server standing in for PostgREST** (the slate names this shape). The real substrate is not written to tonight. |\n| `TestMigration0088IdentityCodesDownAndUpRoundTrip` | No stub. `db.MigrateTo` / `db.Migrate` on the package database, restored to HEAD. |\n| `TestNothingInThisPackageSends` | No stub; a source walk. No allowlist change. |\n| G1 build + vet; full Go `-p 1` counts | No stub. |\n| `sw.js` idempotent, count 51; full Playwright suite on the merged tree | **Not this card's legs — the orchestrator's**, at the merged HEAD under the lock. Owed. |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2713,"cache_read_input_tokens":167892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2713},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"792dcbd6-aa1d-4c6e-83da-0e3997c4c9b1","uuid":"883069a8-817f-4102-9e2e-e9564127f315","timestamp":"2026-10-05T23:41:47.369Z","request_id":"req_011CfjyVSncuBkyhvY53WqqV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Q71GVoavitRebHxmEJZ2cr":{"file_path":"/home/jcole/projects/hq/.night-crew/runs/20261006/worktrees/identity-code-and-qr/.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/merge-intents/identity-code-and-qr.md","content":"# Merge intent — Card 1 (E1) · `identity