mounted by `MountPublic`** (root router, no session) — a customer's phone\n   and, in Card 2, the carrier fetch the image with no HQ login. Moving it under `Mount` breaks\n   both. Its only secret is the unguessable media id.\n4. **The mint happens AFTER the import transaction commits, one subscriber per transaction**, and\n   a projection that is unconfigured or failing never rolls a mint back: the import answers 200\n   with `warnings:[\"not_projected\"]`.\n5. **Identity-only codes (no first-touch campaign) are never projected** and their payload has no\n   `#o=` fragment. Which campaign such a signup is entitled to is an operator question (the\n   card's PARK note); nothing here guesses one.\n6. **`identity_media.subscriber_id … ON DELETE CASCADE`** — deleting a subscriber deletes their\n   image; that is the erasure path.\n7. **Migration number `0088`**, with its Down.\n8. Card 2 extends `ImportSubscribers` AFTER this card's mint loop; the `signed_up` insert path and\n   the `resend_requested` event are unchanged by this card.\n\n## What is safe to drop\n\n`backend/cmd/qrgen/` is safe to drop only together with `[IC-03]` (its one caller). The evidence\nlogs are safe to drop in the sense that no suite reads them. Nothing else.\n\n## done_when clauses — stubs and fixtures\n\n**The sender stub is the point tonight (D-KR2), and this card has no sender at all**: it mints,\nrenders and projects; nothing is sent, no provider is called, and\n`TestNothingInThisPackageSends` stays green with no allowlist change. Per clause:\n\n| Clause | Rides a stub or fixture? |\n|---|---|\n| `[IC-01]` offline scan of the server-minted PNG → `embeddedOffer` | **Fixture input, real path.** Subscribers come from the committed Fluent Forms fixture (`HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH`), never the live website database; the campaign and its code are seeded by SQL on the e2e database (:5434). The mint, the PNG, the public route and the shipped scanner page are all real. No sender involved. |\n| `[IC-02]` the same PNG online → `offerReady`, source `server` | **Stub — the one permitted one.** The server lookup is answered by `page.route` on the sync door's path (the e2e stack has no substrate), returning the row the projection would have written (id = the uuid-v5 of the subscriber id, the campaign, its `ends_at`). The projection itself is NOT exercised here — `TestProjectIdentityCodeUpserts` covers it against a fake PostgREST. No sender involved. |\n| `[IC-03]` negative control (Medium / version 11) | No stub. The PNG is generated in-test by `backend/cmd/qrgen` with the repo's own `go-qrcode`, scanned through the shipped page. |\n| `TestMintIdentityCodeIsIdempotent`, `TestMintIdentityCodeNoFirstTouchIsIdentityOnly` | No stub. Real Postgres on :5434 (`hq_test_go_e1`). Projection deliberately unconfigured in the second. |\n| `TestProjectIdentityCodeUpserts` | **Stub: an `httptest` server standing in for PostgREST** (the slate names this shape). The real substrate is not written to tonight. |\n| `TestMigration0088IdentityCodesDownAndUpRoundTrip` | No stub. `db.MigrateTo` / `db.Migrate` on the package database, restored to HEAD. |\n| `TestNothingInThisPackageSends` | No stub; a source walk. No allowlist change. |\n| G1 build + vet; full Go `-p 1` counts | No stub. |\n| `sw.js` idempotent, count 51; full Playwright suite on the merged tree | **Not this card's legs — the orchestrator's**, at the merged HEAD under the lock. Owed. |\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
