{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5BWYnbxiVhJ9omWwed","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01StDNNyoKMaxXxExb63DBDr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sleep 2; pgrep -af \"e1-seam.sh|playwright test marketing\" | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/merge-intents/identity-code-and-qr.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\n## Facts at the end of the card — 🛑 PARKED, work preserved\n\n**The card is built as specified and reported `halt`.** The Go gates are green; the three\nPlaywright gates cannot be honestly reported green, because the measurement they rest on does not\nhold. Nothing above changed except as listed here.\n\n### Why it is parked (the operator's question is in the result contract)\n\nThe signed encoding correction says: a Low / QR-version-9 code is read by the shipped scanner from\na photo, a Medium / version-11 code is not, and widening the scan surface buys headroom. Over 250\nfreshly drawn codes (`logs/identity-code-and-qr/density-probe.log`):\n\n| What a crew member photographs | Read | Not read |\n|---|---|---|\n| the card's code (Low, version 9, full offer inside) | 212 of 250 — 85% | about 1 in 7, and the same code fails every time |\n| the \"negative control\" (Medium, version 11) | 208 of 250 — 83% | — it reads as often as the card's own |\n| a code with no offer inside (identity-only, version 3) | 93/100, 143/150 | about 1 in 17 |\n| same codes, scan surface 320 px vs 640 px vs 1280 px | identical | the SAME codes fail at every width |\n\nSo `[IC-03]` as signed is false on most runs, `[IC-01]` / `[IC-02]` pass only when the token just\nminted happens to draw a readable symbol, and the 640 px widening does nothing measurable. No\ndecode ever produced another customer's token. The live-camera path was not measured — no gate\nexercises it.\n\n### Changes to the lists above\n\n- **One more shared file:** `backend/internal/marketing/routes_test.go` —\n  `TestMountPublicRegistersOnlyTheLanding` pinned the public surface at exactly two routes; it is\n  now `TestMountPublicRegistersExactlyThePublicSurface` and pins four (`GET`+`HEAD /q/{short}`,\n  `GET`+`HEAD /m/{id}.png`). Card 2's `POST /sms/inbound` will have to be added to it on purpose.\n- **Not done, because the card did not land:** the roadmap line is still `PLANNED`; the\n  `night-crew.toml` roll-call comment is still 7 (the new spec joins the `marketing` seam by\n  filename the moment it is on a branch — whoever lands it moves the comment to 8).\n- **`tests/marketing-identity.spec.js` is left as the signed gates, with a header that says what\n  was measured.** Landing it unchanged puts a mostly-red `[IC-03]` and two one-in-seven-red tests\n  into the suite; with the config's one retry they would mostly pass, which is worse.\n- **Decided at engineer level, for ratification (delegation/P-1):**\n  1. the QR never encodes above version 10 — a long `offer_text` has its embedded label shortened\n     with \"…\" (the spec says label = `offer_text`; an ordinary offer line is untouched);\n  2. `identity_code.media_url` is a relative path (`/m/<id>.png`), like `png_url` on a campaign\n     code; Card 2 will need to prefix a public host for the carrier;\n  3. `expires_at` in the QR is the campaign's end date in UTC;\n  4. an import whose new subscriber could not be minted answers 200 with a second warning,\n     `identity_not_minted` (the spec names only `not_projected`);\n  5. `not_projected` is reported only when a code that HAS a campaign was not projected; after the\n     first projection failure in one import the rest are skipped, not retried one by one;\n  6. the uuid-v5 name is `https://hq.yumyums.kitchen/identity-code/<subscriber id>` in the RFC URL\n     namespace; the token alphabet has 31 symbols (the spec's string), about 79 bits.\n- **Known gap, not in the spec:** a code that was minted but not projected is never projected\n  again (no column records it, and only NEW subscribers are minted on import). Subscribers who\n  existed before migration 0088 get no code from any path in this card.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Confirm the seam run is alive and append the end-of-card facts to the merge-intent note"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":472,"cache_read_input_tokens":321305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":472},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"792dcbd6-aa1d-4c6e-83da-0e3997c4c9b1","uuid":"15872ebb-963e-4646-bd27-cbad68ae997f","timestamp":"2026-10-06T00:56:05.934Z","request_id":"req_011Cfk5BViSED7JUDttsMARa","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01StDNNyoKMaxXxExb63DBDr":{"command":"sleep 2; pgrep -af \"e1-seam.sh|playwright test marketing\" | head -5; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/merge-intents/identity-code-and-qr.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns+='''\n## Facts at the end of the card — 🛑 PARKED, work preserved\n\n**The card is built as specified and reported `halt`.** The Go gates are green; the three\nPlaywright gates cannot be honestly reported green, because the measurement they rest on does not\nhold. Nothing above changed except as listed here.\n\n### Why it is parked (the operator's question is in the result contract)\n\nThe signed encoding correction says: a Low / QR-version-9 code is read by the shipped scanner from\na photo, a Medium / version-11 code is not, and widening the scan surface buys headroom. Over 250\nfreshly drawn codes (`logs/identity-code-and-qr/density-probe.log`):\n\n| What a crew member photographs | Read | Not read |\n|---|---|---|\n| the card's code (Low, version 9, full offer inside) | 212 of 250 — 85% | about 1 in 7, and the same code fails every time |\n| the \"negative control\" (Medium, version 11) | 208 of 250 — 83% | — it reads as often as the card's own |\n| a code with no offer inside (identity-only, version 3) | 93/100, 143/150 | about 1 in 17 |\n| same codes, scan surface 320 px vs 640 px vs 1280 px | identical | the SAME codes fail at every width |\n\nSo `[IC-03]` as signed is false on most runs, `[IC-01]` / `[IC-02]` pass only when the token just\nminted happens to draw a readable symbol, and the 640 px widening does nothing measurable. No\ndecode ever produced another customer's token. The live-camera path was not measured — no gate\nexercises it.\n\n### Changes to the lists above\n\n- **One more shared file:** `backend/internal/marketing/routes_test.go` —\n  `TestMountPublicRegistersOnlyTheLanding` pinned the public surface at exactly two routes; it is\n  now `TestMountPublicRegistersExactlyThePublicSurface` and pins four (`GET`+`HEAD /q/{short}`,\n  `GET`+`HEAD /m/{id}.png`). Card 2's `POST /sms/inbound` will have to be added to it on purpose.\n- **Not done, because the card did not land:** the roadmap line is still `PLANNED`; the\n  `night-crew.toml` roll-call comment is still 7 (the new spec joins the `marketing` seam by\n  filename the moment it is on a branch — whoever lands it moves the comment to 8).\n- **`tests/marketing-identity.spec.js` is left as the signed gates, with a header that says what\n  was measured.** Landing it unchanged puts a mostly-red `[IC-03]` and two one-in-seven-red tests\n  into the suite; with the config's one retry they would mostly pass, which is worse.\n- **Decided at engineer level, for ratification (delegation/P-1):**\n  1. the QR never encodes above version 10 — a long `offer_text` has its embedded label shortened\n     with \"…\" (the spec says label = `offer_text`; an ordinary offer line is untouched);\n  2. `identity_code.media_url` is a relative path (`/m/<id>.png`), like `png_url` on a campaign\n     code; Card 2 will need to prefix a public host for the carrier;\n  3. `expires_at` in the QR is the campaign's end date in UTC;\n  4. an import whose new subscriber could not be minted answers 200 with a second warning,\n     `identity_not_minted` (the spec names only `not_projected`);\n  5. `not_projected` is reported only when a code that HAS a campaign was not projected; after the\n     first projection failure in one import the rest are skipped, not retried one by one;\n  6. the uuid-v5 name is `https://hq.yumyums.kitchen/identity-code/<subscriber id>` in the RFC URL\n     namespace; the token alphabet has 31 symbols (the spec's string), about 79 bits.\n- **Known gap, not in the spec:** a code that was minted but not projected is never projected\n  again (no column records it, and only NEW subscribers are minted on import). Subscribers who\n  existed before migration 0088 get no code from any path in this card.\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF","description":"Confirm the seam run is alive and append the end-of-card facts to the merge-intent note"}}}
