{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfk5rDsXNFCxRFNJoUtFv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I built the card as specified, but I'm reporting it as a park (`halt`), not as completed. The working tree is left intact and nothing is committed.\n\n## Why it's parked\n\nThe signed encoding rests on a premise that doesn't hold: that a Low/version-9 code reads from a photo and a Medium/version-11 one doesn't. The spike drew one symbol per variant. I measured 250 freshly drawn codes through the shipped page's decoder:\n\n| What gets photographed | Read |\n|---|---|\n| The card's code (Low, version 9, offer inside) | 212 of 250 (85%) |\n| The \"negative control\" (Medium, version 11) | 208 of 250 (83%) |\n| A bare identity-only code (version 3) | about 94% |\n| Same codes at surface widths 320 to 1280 px | identical; the same codes fail at every width |\n\n- **What a crew member sees:** about one customer code in seven is not read by \"Scan from photo\", and the same code fails every time.\n- **The 640 px widening:** it changes nothing measurable.\n- **Safety:** no decode ever produced another customer's token.\n- **Not measured:** the live-camera path (no gate exercises it) and any other decoder.\n\nConsequences for the gates:\n- **`[IC-03]`** (Medium renders no offer) is false on most runs. It passed once and failed once tonight, on different tokens.\n- **`[IC-01]` / `[IC-02]`** pass only when the token just minted happens to draw a readable symbol. They passed in both runs tonight. The config's one retry mints a new token, so it would mostly hide a miss.\n\nI did not rewrite the gates or pin a token to get a green. The spec file carries a header saying what was measured.\n\n## What was run\n\n- **Red-first:** shown for Go (build failure) and Playwright (3 failed; the pre-change binary answers `/m/<uuid>.png` with 404).\n- **Named Go tests:** the four identity tests, `TestNothingInThisPackageSends` and four riders, 9 of 9 pass, with no egress-allowlist change.\n- **Build and vet:** exit 0.\n- **Full Go suite, `-p 1`, under the lock:** 15 packages ok; 463 top-level pass, 0 fail, 3 skip (opt-in live-substrate legs); `TestRowVisibilityRLS` pass.\n- **Marketing seam subset, no retries:** 132 tests, 131 pass, 1 fail (`[IC-03]`, because the Medium control was read).\n- **Repo-hygiene spec:** 5 of 5.\n- **Not run (the orchestrator's):** the full Playwright suite, and `sw.js` regeneration with the precache count.\n\nNothing in the diff sends or can reach a provider. Stubs: the projection test uses a fake PostgREST, `[IC-02]` uses the one permitted `page.route` lookup, and subscribers come from the committed Fluent Forms fixture.\n\n## Decision for the operator\n\nAs the owner, I want every customer who is sent a code to be readable at the window, so that nobody holding a valid code is turned away. Which do you want?\n\n- **A. Land as built.** Treat photo-scan as best-effort and rely on the live camera; drop `[IC-03]` and restate the other two as what is true.\n- **B. Put less in the QR.** Without the campaign id the read rate is about 97%, but I have not checked what the scanner loses offline without it.\n- **C. Fix the scanner's photo decoder first, then land this unchanged.** The shipped reader misses about 1 in 17 even on the simplest code.\n- **D. Have the server check each code is readable before issuing it.** This needs a decoder on the server that the repo doesn't have.\n\nI recommend C, with an attended camera test at the truck first, because the floor is in the reader and not in this card's encoding.\n\n## For triage\n\n- **Card 2** (`mms-send-on-signup`) should not start on this.\n- **Engineer-level calls for ratification** are listed in the merge-intent note. The main one: a long offer line is shortened inside the QR so the symbol never exceeds version 10.\n- **Out-of-footprint edits**, also listed there:\n  - `playwright.config.js` gains `HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH` so the e2e server can import the committed fixture.\n  - The public-surface guard in `routes_test.go` now pins four routes.\n  - One status assertion each in `subscribers_test.go` and `marketing-subscribers.spec.js` moves from `not_sent` to `minted`.\n- **Known gap:** a code minted but not projected is never re-projected, and subscribers who existed before migration 0088 get no code.\n- **Not flipped:** the roadmap line stays `PLANNED` and the `night-crew.toml` roll-call comment stays at 7, because nothing landed.\n- **Screenshot-restore rule is one directory short:** the seam leg also rewrote seven committed PNGs under `runs/2026-10-02-autonomous/logs/h5/states/`. I restored them; the launch prompt's command names only `h4/states/`.\n\nEvidence is under `.night-crew/runs/2026-10-06-autonomous/logs/identity-code-and-qr/`; start with `density-probe.log`. The result contract is at `/home/jcole/projects/hq/.night-crew/runs/20261006/identity-code-and-qr/attempt-1/result.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3078,"cache_read_input_tokens":331249,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3078},"output_tokens":761,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"792dcbd6-aa1d-4c6e-83da-0e3997c4c9b1","uuid":"1d6bd782-02b7-459b-8af1-c27cde72267c","timestamp":"2026-10-06T01:04:48.589Z","request_id":"req_011Cfk5rCxCbMK3B3TqgFJJe"}
